---
import MainLayout from "../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import img1 from "../../images/comics/abyss-1.jpg";
import img2 from "../../images/comics/abyss-2.jpg";
import img3 from "../../images/comics/abyss-3.jpg";
import img4 from "../../images/comics/abyss-4.jpg";
import img5 from "../../images/comics/abyss-5.jpg";
import img6 from "../../images/comics/og-abyss-zine.jpg";

const pages = [
  { src: img1, alt: "Abyss Page 1" },
  { src: img2, alt: "Abyss Page 2" },
  { src: img3, alt: "Abyss Page 3" },
  { src: img4, alt: "Abyss Page 4" },
  { src: img5, alt: "Abyss Page 5" },
];

const wippages = [
  { src: img6, alt: "Abyss WIP 1" },
];
---
<MainLayout title="Abyss | Zine">
    <section class="container">
        <h1 class="title heading">Abyss</h1>
        <div class="image-list">
            {pages.map((page) => (
                <Image src={page.src} alt={page.alt} />
            ))}
        </div>
        <h3>Digital, Riso-printed</h3>
        <p>
            This is a zine I created to be riso-printed and also shared at DC Zinefest in 2026.
        </p>
        <p>
            
        </p>
        <div class="image-list">
            {wippages.map((page) => (
                <Image src={page.src} alt={page.alt} />
            ))}
        </div>
        <h3>Process</h3>
        <p>I started off with writing the script and drew rough thumbnails based on it. After that, I arranged the thumbnails into a one-page zine format and finished it how I normally world, while paying attention to textures and color contrast. Through Spectrolite, I found a color combination that I liked, and would periodically check the colors while finishing the zine. Finally, I calibrated files and handled the riso-printing process at a local print studio.</p>
    </section>
</MainLayout>
<style>
.container {
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 2rem;
    text-align: left;
}
img {
    max-width: 500px;
    max-height: 300px;
    width: auto;
    height: auto;
}
.image-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    grid-gap: 1rem;
    justify-content: left;
}
</style>